S

#29001
"Southern Edge of a Great Winter Plain"
"Apparently the prime hunting ground for an enormous predator, the snow of this

area is covered in large bear tracks, mostly leading south and east from

here.  The snow has been dug away in places, leaving holes deep enough for a

man to stand in.  A single patch of bright, red blood dots the snow, packed

under an undisturbed footprint.  Off to the west, a misstep will carry the

unmindful traveller to their death at the bottom of a drop into white

nothingness.  A narrowing ridge leads southward, sloping down and off the

plateau to the unknown below.

"
"[Nereus] beary good hunting ground

[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
