#29003
"South End of a Great Wintry Plain"
"Snow deep enough to cover a man completely blankets this desolate area.  Deep

trails dug by the movement of some great beast lead through the snow to the

north, west, and south; the remainder of the snow is fairly easy to travel on

because of a thick crust of ice which has formed atop it.  Tracks of wolves

are also in evidence in the dug tracks, but it is impossible to make out more

tracks on the frozen crust of the rest of the snow.  The plateau continues in

all directions from here, though to the south and east looms the edge of this

wintry plain.

"
"[Nereus] entering code here to activate the fox

[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
