#29007
"Southwestern Edge of a Great Wintry Plain"
"Before the sinkhole to the northwest opened up, it appears that the plateau

stretched off to the west another couple hundred feet.  Now, only a narrow

ridge of rock is traversable, a balancing act above two gorges.  The snow in

this region has been well-packed down and shows the tracks of several species

of animals, from tiny fox and rabbit tracks to the massive indentations of

what looks to be an elephant.  The animals seem to sense the danger of the

terrain to the south and west; there is a lip of undisturbed snow before the

cliff edge to the south and the ridge to the west.  For as far as the eye can

see to the south, the peaks of the Dragonspires dot the horizon.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

"
