#29012
"Narrow Trail - Hugging the Moutainside"
"Caught between a deep sinkhole to the south and a steep, ice-slicked cliff

wall to the north, a trail here has been formed by the passage of dozens of

padded, dog-like feet, hugging the cliff wall.  Near the rim of the sinkhole,

fresh snow has fallen and lays undisturbed by any animal activity.  The trail

seems to abruptly stop as the cliff wall falls away to the west; perhaps there

is some reason the animals avoid that area.

"
