#29013
"Western Edge of a Great Winter Plain"
"Sheer cliffs rise to the northwest on what now has become the western edge of

this wintry plateau.  A great sinkhole has opened up to the southwest, leaving

only a narrow, snow-covered ridge to the west of here.  The tracks of what

appear to be several very large wolves, moving together, are visible in the

snow and hugging the cliffside to the northwest -- perhaps this is their

hunting area or on the way to it.  Deep drifts have collected to the north;

game trails of packed down snow cut through the drifts, almost if this is the

only safe route to take further north.

"
""
