#29014
"Rim of a Great Sinkhole"
"Despite the appearance of a great deal of animal activity, the wildlife

appears to stop well away from the western edge of this snowy plain, where a

sinkhole has opened up and swallowed the plateau.  Trails are visible running

north-south, and a fainter trail leading east, packed down by the travel of a

variety of wildlife.  The snow is fairly deep here, and has piled in an

undisturbed lip on the western edge before the steep drop to the bottom of the

sinkhole.  Despite the peaks that rise up along the western edge of the

plateau a bit north of here, the mighty frozen wall still dominates the

landscape, visible far in the distance to the north.

"
