east of the plain.  Waist-deep snow, covered quickly from fresh snow blowing

down from the cliff to the east, has seen animal traffic in the very recent

past.  The tracks are obviously those of a very large creature, but more than

that is difficult to make out because of the new-fallen snow that dusts them. 

