#29017
"Dragonspire Plateau - Windswept Ice"
"Scoured clean to a rock-like sheet of opaque ice, this windswept section of

the plateau is truly inhospitable.  Evidence of the travel of great, heavy

creatures is present here: the ice is starred in places; in others, it has

been marked with claws.  Sweeping from east to west, the wind swoops down from

the cliffs to the east and north, tumbling west along the plateau, and

carrying all the powdery snow with it.  Deep drifts of powder have collected

to the west along a steep cliff face.  The ice sheet continues to the east and

north; to the north, the ice seems thin and brittle and appears to be avoided

by the wildlife.

"
