#29044
"Before a Marvelous Tree of Ice"
"A mighty tree made of ice grows here from beneath the snow, perfect in every

detail.  Waist-deep snow covers this section of the plain, but has been

tracked down by extremely heavy animal traffic leading in all directions. 

Strangely, despite all the animal traffic in the region, a ring a few feet

wide is completely undisturbed around the base of the tree.  It would appear

that nothing, animal or man, has touched or climbed the tree since this snow

began falling.  To the south and east, cliffs form the eastern edge of this

wintry plateau; to the north, the might of the frozen wall dwarfs this tree of

ice.

"
