#29047
"Upon a Frozen Lake - Northwestern Corner of the Plateau"
"This bleak corner of the plain seems to be dominated utterly by the frozen

wall, which towers over this corner of the plateau.  Even the wind is stilled

here and sound seems muted.  From this close, it is evident that the wall is

not an ordinary glacier or purely natural phenomenon: the ice is a soft,

opaque blue-white, and the surface of the wall is perfectly smooth, almost as

if it were planed stone.  A thin layer of crusted, old snow covers the surface

of the lake, the occasional track visible; it has been long since any new snow

fell here.  The frozen lake continues from here, to the south and east.

"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **

