next, the crunching of hard-packed snow.  Incomprehensibly tall, the frozen

wall stretches for what seems like eternity to the east and west,

mirror-smooth.  To the east, past the shore of the lake, a man-sized wall of

snow has been piled around a magnificent archway carved into the wall itself. 

The frozen surface of the lake stretches out to the west and south, exposed

ice glinting softly in the light.

"
