#29054
"Beneath a Great Archway - Tunnel into the Ice"
"A grand archway arcs overhead, twenty feet in height at the tallest point.  A

level covering of snow blankets the ground here, having been blown in softly

from the plateau to the south.  The glimmering, opaque ice of the outside of

the wall is also present here in this tunnel through the wall; the walls of

the ice cave are perfectly smooth and the curve of the arch is flawless and

gentle.  To the north, this tunnel intersects an east-south tunnel, where an

