#29057
"Bottom of the Frozen Lake - Hot Spring"
"From what little light filters down from through the icy water above, you can

make out great stalagmites along the bottom of the lake floor.  Furnaces of

geothermal heat, these hot springs emit clouds of choking brimstone and waves

of scalding heat.  Above, the water is also thawed; these hot springs must be

the source that allows this passage through the frozen lake to exist as

water.  In all directions but up, the water has frozen to ice, creating this

well of thawed water.

"
