#29058
"Atop a Frozen Waterfall - Overlooking the Plateau"
"Once, a great river flowed from a gaping hole in the grey rock of the cliff

face to the west.  Now, it has frozen into a great sheet of ice, lightly

dusted with powdery snow fallen from above.  When the river flowed, it might

have been thirty feet across and flowed for twenty feet before tumbling into

the lake below.  There is a grand view of the Dragonspire plateau to the east

from this perch, as well as the legendary frozen wall.

"
""
