#29059
"Wide Mountain Ledge - Parallel with the Frozen Wall"
"This ledge along the grey cliff wall is wide and level, offering plenty of

room to move about, or room to set up camp and take some well-needed rest. 

Probably twenty paces across, the ledge seems almost like a trail as it slopes

slightly upwards as it continues to the north.  Snow has collected at the base

of the cliff ledge here, although there are a few enormous, cat-like prints

smashed into the snow -- evidence that this ledge is probably not the best

resting place after all.  In terms of elevation, this cliffside trail is

parallel with the frozen wall, allowing the first glimpse at what lies

beyond.  Off the cliff edge to the east, a frozen waterfall is visible, caught

in foamy whiteness as it froze; to the south the ledge abruptly plunges into

white nothingness.

"
"[Nereus] Bleeding to death acode here, don't move it please

"
