#29060
"Mountain Ledge Overlooking the Frozen Wall"
"Midway up this wide, sloping mountain ledge, travellers can finally reach a

vantage point above the frozen wall.  Almost immediately to the east and

perhaps a hundred feet below, the frozen wall stretches east for miles, and

north for as far as the eye can see.  Strangely, the mountain ledge seems to

have seen much activity; despite fresh snowfall, enormous, cat-like prints are

evident, churning up the snow at your feet.  The ledge continues its slope

upward to the north, and slopes gently downward to the south.

"
