#29061
"Mountain Ledge - Handholds in a Cliff Face"
"Whether this ledge was once part of a mountain road for travellers is now

unclear; but it appears likely that this was a known route, because hand and

foot holds have been scraped into the cliff face to the north.  The snow here

shows continued signs of the activity of a large animal or animals, but the

dusting of snow here is too light to make out any more details.  This rock

ledge slopes downward while it hugs the mountainside to the south, while to

the east and far below, the frozen wall stretches; unbroken ice which

continues for miles.


An ancient stone marker which has been deliberately defaced lies mostly

covered by snow.

"
