#29062
"Mountain Ledge Hugging the Cliff Face"
"Narrower than the ledge below, this section of the ledge appears to have

partially collapsed along its eastern edge some time ago.  Still nearly twenty

paces across from the western cliff face to the eastern edge, the ledge is

level and offers an easy rest after a tiring climb.  Barely visible through

the light dusting of snow here are the prints of some massive, clawed beast. 

The prints seem very fresh, and also whatever made them seems to either

frequent the area or travel in groups.  To the south, the ledge ends abruptly,

but the cliff face appears to have had handholds carved into it, making for an

easy climb down to another ledge twenty feet below.  The frozen wall,

implacable and incomprehensibly large, stretches out below the cliff edge for

dozens of miles.

"
