#29064
"A Warm Cavern"
"Substantially warmer than the narrow ledge just outside, this shallow cave

appears to serve as a den for some sort of large, predatory mammals.  Once a

natural cavern perhaps ten feet tall and just as deep, the grey stone floor

has been worn smooth by the tread of countless feet and the walls worn smooth.

The cavern wall at the back is hot to the touch, spreading a gentle warmth

throughout the cavern.  A narrow, ice-rimed fissure leads back into the cold

to the west.  Small animal bones and patches of fur litter the cavern floor,

further evidence this small cave is used as a den.

"
