#29065
"Mountain Ledge - Sheltered Alcove"
"What might have once been a resting place for travellers along this mountain

road has become something much more alarming: it appears this is a center of

activity for whatever predators roam this part of the mountain.  The trail is

wider here, and a sheltered alcove is evident on the western side of the ledge

alongside the cliff face.  A slight overhang offers solace from the wind and

snow falling from above.  Something has been digging in the stone to the west,

clawing out chunks of the rock itself.  Further evidence of activity can be

found; sticky, black droplets of blood are visible smeared along the wall of

the alcove.  A brisk wind keeps the ledge here free of ice and snow, which

coats the trail more as it slopes upward to the north and downward to the

south.

"
